| 10.6 | Ticket status transitions (`waiting_on_approval`, etc.) | F9 | |
| 10.7 | CD-1002 pauses with `waiting_on_approval` + `approval_requests` row | F9 | |
| 10.8 | Approve resumes and runs refund tool once | F9 | |
| 10.9 | Reject routes to escalation | F9 | |
| 10.10 | Second run during pause returns 409 | F9 | |
| 10.11 | Resume of non-paused run returns 409 | F9 | |
| 10.12 | CD-1005, CD-1006, CD-1009, CD-1011 escalate without approval wait | F10 | |
| 10.13 | CD-1013 does not take export action | N4 | |
| 10.14 | Risk high for approval-required plans, policy escalation, critical severity, injection, failed output validation | F9, N5 | |
| 10.15 | Create `scripts/demo.py` + `make demo [TICKET=]` | F9, F10 | ✅ |
| 10.16 | Create `tests/workflow/` pause/resume/rejection/GDPR escalation tests | F9, F10 | |

**Exit criteria:** Code before `interrupt()` idempotent. Approved and automatic paths share `ToolRegistry.execute`. Viewer gets 403 on run/approve/reject.

