## Requirement Traceability

| ID | Requirement | Proven by phase |
|----|-------------|-----------------|
| F1 | Create ticket via POST /api/v1/tickets | 4 |
| F2 | Classify into 10 categories + summary | 8, 13 |
| F3 | Severity low/medium/high/critical with reason | 7, 8 |
| F4 | Load customer, subscription, workspace, tickets, memory | 4, 8, 11 |
| F5 | Cited evidence from hybrid retrieval | 5, 8, 13 |
| F6 | Similar previously resolved cases | 5, 8 |
| F7 | Diagnosis: probable causes + numbered steps | 8 |
| F8 | Resolution plan: summary, reply, notes, actions | 8, 13 |
| F9 | Consequential actions need human approval | 6, 10 |
| F10 | Escalate policy cases to named team | 7, 10, 13 |
| F11 | Ticket summary + memory update after every run | 9, 11 |
| F12 | Approve/reject/escalate/reply/request-info from one screen | 12 |
| F13 | Every node/tool/LLM call inspectable | 9 |
| F14 | Runs offline in DEMO_MODE with no API key | 1, 13 |
| N1 | JWT auth (Supabase-compatible HS256) | 3 |
| N2 | Rate limiting fixed window in Redis | 3 |
| N3 | X-Request-ID on every response | 1 |
| N4 | Ticket text treated as data (prompt injection defence) | 7, 10 |
| N5 | Output validation before reply reaches customer | 7 |
| N6 | Audit every non-GET request | 3 |
| N7 | No secrets in memory notes | 7, 11 |
| N8 | Deployable as containers to AWS, Azure, GCP | 13 |

---

## Commands

```bash
make setup            # .venv + deps + .env
make seed             # load sample data into DB
make ingest           # chunk + index knowledge base
make backend          # FastAPI on :8000
make demo             # CD-1002 refund end-to-end (pauses for approval)
make demo TICKET=CD-1005  # escalation demo
make test             # backend pytest (~6s, offline)
make lint             # ruff
make smoke            # BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 make smoke
```
